ets that should be encapsulated must be routed to that interface.
MPLS routes may be created using sockaddrs  for  destination  and
tag  fields.   Other  protocols  can be encapsulated using routes
pointing to mpls pseudo‐interfaces, and sockaddrs for tags.   De‐
capsulation  can  be  made using values of reserved labels set in
the tag field (see below).  For more information about doing this
using userland utilities see the section  of  this  manual  page.
